{"name":"Witch Hazel","hex":"#fbf073","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"witch hazel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several small deciduous trees, of the genus Hamamelis, having yellow flowers","Hamamelis vernalis, native to the Ozarks."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/witch_hazel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Witch Hazel (Looney Tunes)","blocks":[{"text":"Witch Hazel is an animated cartoon character in the Warner Bros. Looney Tunes and Merrie Melodies series of cartoons and TV shows. Witch Hazel is a fairy tale witch antagonist with green skin, a round figure, exaggerated bulbous facial features, and a single tooth. The name is a pun on the witch-hazel plant and folk remedies based on it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f3/Witch_Hazel_%28Looney_Tunes%29.jpg/330px-Witch_Hazel_%28Looney_Tunes%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Witch_Hazel_(Looney_Tunes)"},{"title":"Witch-hazel","blocks":[{"text":"Witch-hazels or witch hazels (Hamamelis) are a genus of flowering plants in the family Hamamelidaceae, with three species in North America, and one each in Japan (H. japonica) and China (H. mollis). The North American species are occasionally called winterbloom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Hamamelis_virginiana_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-070.jpg/330px-Hamamelis_virginiana_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-070.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Witch-hazel"},{"title":"Hazel","blocks":[{"text":"Hazels are plants of the genus Corylus of deciduous trees and large shrubs native to the temperate Northern Hemisphere. The genus is usually placed in the birch family, Betulaceae, though some botanists split the hazels into a separate family Corylaceae. The fruit of the hazel is the hazelnut; the trees are also grown as ornaments in hedges or gardens."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Corylus_avellana_0001.JPG/330px-Corylus_avellana_0001.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazel"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f3/Witch_Hazel_%28Looney_Tunes%29.jpg/330px-Witch_Hazel_%28Looney_Tunes%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f3/Witch_Hazel_%28Looney_Tunes%29.jpg/330px-Witch_Hazel_%28Looney_Tunes%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWitch_Hazel_(Looney_Tunes).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/60/Witch_Hazel_transformed.png/330px-Witch_Hazel_transformed.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/60/Witch_Hazel_transformed.png/330px-Witch_Hazel_transformed.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Transformed into a female rabbit, Witch Hazel gets Bugs Bunny's attention in Bewitched Bunny (1954)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWitch_Hazel_transformed.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Hamamelis_virginiana_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-070.jpg/330px-Hamamelis_virginiana_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-070.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Hamamelis_virginiana_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-070.jpg/330px-Hamamelis_virginiana_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-070.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://e